From: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] agm: allow ATS initialization in unprivileged sessions

Unprivileged desktop sessions cannot create an explicitly scheduled FIFO
thread. Retry the optional ATS control thread with normal scheduling on EPERM.
Other thread failures remain errors. This does not bypass DSP initialization.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>

--- a/service/src/agm.c
+++ b/service/src/agm.c
@@ -161,6 +161,13 @@
     if (enable_ats_thread) {
         ret = pthread_create(&ats_thread, (const pthread_attr_t *) &tattr,
                                            ats_init_thread, NULL);
+        /* ATS is a control thread. Desktop sessions may lack permission for
+         * SCHED_FIFO; keep control initialization available at normal priority.
+         */
+        if (ret == EPERM) {
+            AGM_LOGI("ATS realtime scheduling unavailable, using default policy");
+            ret = pthread_create(&ats_thread, NULL, ats_init_thread, NULL);
+        }
         if (ret) {
             AGM_LOGE("ats init thread creation failed");
             ats_thread_started = false;
